          up: {"title":"Match the meeting document (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>Harder: each card is an extract or a description from the Business Club's papers. Match each document or term to it.</p>","pairs":[{"l":"Notice of meeting","r":"\"The next ordinary meeting will be held in Room B12 on Thursday 5 November 2026 at 3.15 pm.\""},{"l":"Agenda","r":"\"1 Apologies for absence 2 Minutes of the last meeting 3 Matters arising\""},{"l":"Chairman's agenda","r":"\"5 Treasurer's report: balance EC$640\", beside a blank column headed NOTES"},{"l":"Minutes","r":"\"It was agreed that the Club would sell coconut tarts.\""},{"l":"Action items","r":"\"Obtain prices from two bakeries | Jaylen Hodge | 12 November\""},{"l":"Matters arising","r":"The agenda item where members report on tasks from the last meeting"},{"l":"Any other business","r":"The agenda item where a member raises the broken laboratory tap, which was not listed"},{"l":"Apologies for absence","r":"The first agenda item, recording members who sent word that they could not attend"},{"l":"Quorum","r":"The minimum number of members who must be present for decisions to count"}],"win":"Well matched. You can recognise each document from an extract and explain what each standard agenda item is for."}
